==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|uacuus}} {{qualifier|some Latin texts use the same character for 'u' and 'v'}}
* {{alter|la|vaquus||Vulgar or Late Latin|Appendix Probi}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*wakowos}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|la|vacō|uus|t1=I am empty, void|t2=adjective-forming suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vacuus|eccl=yes}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|vacuus}}

# {{l|en|empty}}, {{l|en|vacant}}, {{l|en|unoccupied}}
#: {{ux|la|Fēmina dīxit pōculum '''vacuum''' esse.|The woman said that the cup was '''empty'''.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|2|quote=Terra [[autem]] erat [[inānis]] et [[vacuus|vacua]], et [[tenebrae]] erant super [[facies|faciem]] [[abyssus|abyssī]] et [[spīritus]] Deī [[fero|ferēbātur]] super [[aqua|aquās]].|trans=And the earth was void and '''empty''', and darkness was upon the face of the deep; and the spirit of God moved over the waters.}}
# [[devoid]] or [[free]] of, [[without]]
# {{lb|la|of time}} [[free]], unoccupied

